Input widths {'a': 1}; output widths {'q': 3}. Clock clk; sample after the posedge edge has settled. Each row's values are driven before the sampled edge. Optional mid input changes occur AFTER sampling, before the other edge, and are carried to the start of the next row. Protocol seed 20261120.
Write a compact JSON Veri-Sure B.1 contract with module_name (top_module), io list with name, dir, width, description, clocking {clock:{name,edge} or null, reset:{name,active,kind} or null}, timing {outputs:{name:{latency_cycles:nonnegative integer}}}, functional_summary {overview, rules}. Public interface must match (include the clock in io).

